# `constitution init --source-tracking` end-to-end (issues #17/#18/#19/#20):
# init writes sourceTracking straight from flags — no post-init hand-edit —
# and the seeded founding ADR carries the reserved `source: bootstrap` value,
# which bypasses the configured pattern check even though jira's default
# pattern would otherwise reject a bare title-derived source. guard stays
# clean afterward.

env CONSTITUTION_TODAY=2026-07-02

exec constitution init --source-tracking jira --founding-file founding.md
stdout 'init: constitution ready'
! stderr .

grep 'type: jira' constitution.yml

exec constitution guard
stdout 'clean'

grep 'source: bootstrap' constitution/adr/ADR-0001-founding-constitution.md

-- founding.md --
## Context and Problem Statement

Established at project bootstrap by `constitution init`.

## Considered Options

- Adopt this founding decision
- Leave the convention implicit

## Decision Outcome

Every change ships with tests, no exceptions.
